.TH CHMAP_GET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chmap_get \- get value by key (type-safe, returns value)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chashmap.h>

value = chmap_get(hm_name, key);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-safe wrapper for chmap_get_elem_ref() that returns the actual value.
Calls ccol_fatal_err() if key not found or size mismatch.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name  Hash map to search
key      Key to look up
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns value associated with key
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Terminates program if key not found
Terminates program if the stored value's size does not match the
size of the declared value type
Returns value, not pointer
For strings, returns the char* itself
For a float or double key, see chmap_construct(3) for the map's
key equality contract (bitwise, except -0.0 canonicalized to 0.0)
For a long double key, see chmap_construct(3) for the map's key
equality contract (value-based, unlike every other key type)
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
chmap_construct(map, int, char*);
int key = 42;
chmap_insert(map, key, "hello");
char* val = chmap_get(map, key); // val is "hello"
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chmap_get_ptr (3),
.BR chmap_insert (3),
.BR chmap_construct (3)
